WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.911
Week 26: Conditional, Courtesy, and Hypothesis. make a tactful request evaluate options state hypothetical consequences

2
00:00:08.911 --> 00:00:22.177
Operational objective. By the end of this section you can make a tactful request, evaluate options, state hypothetical consequences. The focus is useful performance, not isolated terminology.

3
00:00:22.177 --> 00:00:31.409
Language system. Simple conditional; irregular stems; future-in-the-past; conditional courtesy; si + imperfect subjunctive preview.

4
00:00:31.409 --> 00:00:38.208
Sound and delivery. Conditional -ía endings and polite intonation without over-reducing them.

5
00:00:38.208 --> 00:00:47.485
Core principle. Notice meaning first, then form. Retrieve the new language aloud, compare it with the model, and repair one feature at a time.

6
00:00:47.485 --> 00:01:14.916
Model language. Yo elegiría la segunda opción. — I would choose the second option. ¿Podría enviarme los detalles? — Could you send me the details? El cambio reduciría el riesgo. — The change would reduce the risk. Dijo que llegaría al día siguiente. — He or she said that they would arrive the following day. En cambio, ese plan costaría demasiado. — On the other hand, that plan would cost too much.

7
00:01:14.916 --> 00:01:24.814
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
